Validation code generated by validation-gen runs all short circuiting checks before performing the short circuiting. Due to this if multiple shortcricuits checks return errs, all errors are returned. Ideally we should break these shortciruting into two cohorts. One for update operation related one and another one for all others. This aligns well with the handwritten validation code.


```go
// +required
// +listType=map
// +listMapKey=name 1Code has comments. Press enter to view.
// +k8s:required
// +k8s:listType=map
// +k8s:listMapKey=name
// +k8s:maxItems=8
// +k8s:immutable
PodGroups []PodGroup `json:"podGroups" protobuf:"bytes,2,rep,name=podGroups"`
````

In this example +k8s:immutable, +k8s:maxItems=8 and +k8s:required are shortcircuting one.  There is no point in running required and maxItems checks if the field has been modified in update.

